rmal central motor function, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology, abnormal ekg\n\nAcute Mesenteric Ischemia vs Acute Diverticulitis:\n  Favours first:  abnormal bleeding, abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal cornea morphology, abnormal cutaneous elastic fiber morphology, abnormal facial shape\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abdominal tenderness, abnormal basal ganglia mri signal intensity, abnormal central motor function, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology\n\nAcute Mesenteric Ischemia vs Acute Intestinal Obstruction:\n  Favours first:  abnormal bleeding, abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal cornea morphology, abnormal cutaneous elastic fiber morphology, abnormal facial shape\n  Favours second: abdominal distention, abdominal pain, abnormal rectum morphology, abnormality of metabolism/homeostasis, abnormality of the hepatic vasculature\n\nAcute Appendicitis vs Acute Diverticulitis:\n  Favours first:  loss of appetite, malaise, obturator sign, pain with pressure on lower left side, pain worsening with coughing\n  Favours second: abdominal tenderness, bloating, rectal bleeding\n\nAcute Appendicitis vs Acute Intestinal Obstruction:\n  Favours first:  abnormal basal ganglia mri signal intensity, abnormal central motor function, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology, abnormal ekg, abnormal growth hormone level\n  Favours second: abdominal distention, abnormal rectum morphology, abnormality of metabolism/homeostasis, abnormality of the hepatic vasculature, abnormality of the liver\n\nAcute Diverticulitis vs Acute Intestinal Obstruction:\n  Favours first:  abdominal tenderness, abnormal basal ganglia mri signal intensity, abnormal central motor function, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology, abnormal ekg\n  Favours second: abdominal distention, abnormal rectum morphology, abnormality of metabolism/homeostasis, abnormality of the hepatic vasculature, abnormality of the liver\n\nRelated to Acute Gastrointestinal Infection: otitis